IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc-definitions.l4 -- section 2 (definitions) and section 2.1 (further definitions, firearms) of the Criminal Code
-- (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, as defined-term functions. Imports the core (`ccc-core`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to
-- 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French
-- equivalents in parentheses after a defined term are not text to encode and are not quoted as such.
--
-- WHAT A PART CAN DO WITH THIS MODULE: nothing directly. Parts get only `ccc-core` (the lead's merge is what brings this
-- module in), so a part that needs a section 2 term takes its answer as an INPUT named for the section, for example
-- `s 2 peace officer: the victim is one` (PLAN.md lists each such seam). Here the same mechanism is used between terms.
--
-- HOW EACH TERM IS ANSWERED. Every term is a function `s 2 <term>` whose answer is a `MAYBE BOOLEAN`:
--   JUST TRUE    the facts bring the case within the term, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a definition that says "means" and the case is outside it, a condition
--                the text introduces with "if" or "where" that fails, a flat negative ("does not include");
--   NOTHING      not covered: the text says "includes" (or "without restricting the generality") and lists without closing
--                the list, leaves a term undefined, is silent, points outside the sources, or limits a grant in its own words.
-- Every branch that answers JUST FALSE carries a comment that begins FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) and then quotes the words; every
-- branch that answers NOTHING carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Where the facts are a list of kinds, the list is a DECLAREd table: one constructor per member the text names, plus a
-- constructor for "a case the list does not name", which is how the caller says "none of those" without guessing.
-- "Means ... and includes ..." is read as closed (the means part plus the listed extension): see NOTES.md, Marginal readings.

§ `Section 2 -- Definitions ("In this Act,")`

-- Act includes (a) an Act of Parliament, (b) ... former Province of Canada, (c) ... a province, (d) ... in force when a province, territory or place became a province.
-- src:16 | Act includes
-- src:17 | (a) an Act of Parliament,
-- src:18 | (b) an Act of the legislature of the former Province of Canada,
-- src:19 | (c) an Act of the legislature of a province, and
-- src:20 | (d) an Act or ordinance of the legislature of a province, territory or place in force at the time that province, territory or place became a province of Canada; (loi)
@ref s 2 "Act" (src:16-20)
DECLARE `s 2 Act kind` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of Parliament`                                                                       -- (a)
    `an Act of the legislature of the former Province of Canada`                                 -- (b)
    `an Act of the legislature of a province`                                                    -- (c)
    `an Act or ordinance of the legislature of a province, territory or place in force at the time that province, territory or place became a province of Canada`   -- (d)
    `another kind of enactment, not named in the definition of Act`

@ref s 2 "Act" (src:16-20)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 Act kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the legislature of the former Province of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the legislature of a province` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act or ordinance of the legislature of a province, territory or place in force at the time that province, territory or place became a province of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of enactment, not named in the definition of Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Act includes"

-- appearance notice means a notice in Form 9 issued by a peace officer. The second limb is the answer of `s 2 peace officer`, taken as an input.
-- src:21 | appearance notice means a notice in Form 9 issued by a peace officer; (citation à comparaître)
@ref s 2 "appearance notice" (src:21)
GIVEN `the document is a notice in Form 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 appearance notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is a notice in Form 9`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a notice in Form 9"
    ELSE `the issuer is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE for "issued by a peace officer" unmet; NOTHING when the issuer's status is itself undetermined

-- associated personnel means persons who are (a) assigned ..., (b) engaged ..., or (c) deployed ..., to carry out activities in support of the mandate of a UN operation.
-- src:22 | associated personnel means persons who are
-- src:23 | (a) assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations,
-- src:24 | (b) engaged by the Secretary-General of the United Nations, by a specialized agency of the United Nations or by the International Atomic Energy Agency, or
-- src:25 | (c) deployed by a humanitarian non-governmental organization or agency under an agreement with the Secretary-General of the United Nations, by a specialized agency of the United Nations or by the International Atomic Energy Agency,
-- src:26 | to carry out activities in support of the fulfilment of the mandate of a United Nations operation; (personnel associé)
@ref s 2 "associated personnel" (src:22-26)
DECLARE `s 2 associated personnel basis` IS ONE OF
    `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations`   -- (a)
    `engaged by the Secretary-General of the United Nations, by a specialized agency of the United Nations or by the International Atomic Energy Agency`   -- (b)
    `deployed by a humanitarian non-governmental organization or agency under an agreement with the Secretary-General of the United Nations, by a specialized agency of the United Nations or by the International Atomic Energy Agency`   -- (c)
    `appointed in none of the ways (a), (b) or (c) of the definition of associated personnel`

@ref s 2 "associated personnel" (src:22-26)
GIVEN basis IS A `s 2 associated personnel basis`
      `to carry out activities in support of the fulfilment of the mandate of a United Nations operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 associated personnel` MEANS
    IF NOT `to carry out activities in support of the fulfilment of the mandate of a United Nations operation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to carry out activities in support of the fulfilment of the mandate of a United Nations operation"
    ELSE CONSIDER basis
         WHEN `assigned by a government or an intergovernmental organization with the agreement of the competent organ of the United Nations` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `engaged by the Secretary-General of the United Nations, by a specialized agency of the United Nations or by the International Atomic Energy Agency` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `deployed by a humanitarian non-governmental organization or agency under an agreement with the Secretary-General of the United Nations, by a specialized agency of the United Nations or by the International Atomic Energy Agency` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `appointed in none of the ways (a), (b) or (c) of the definition of associated personnel` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "associated personnel means persons who are"

-- Attorney General: (a) with respect to proceedings to which this Act applies, the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province
-- in which they are taken (and, if they are referred to in subsection 2.3(1), also the Attorney General of Canada); (b) the Attorney General
-- of Canada for Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut and for federal proceedings; (c) the Director of Public Prosecutions for the Canada Elections Act.
-- The answer is the list of persons who are "the Attorney General" in those proceedings (the text makes them concurrent in the 2.3(1) cases).
-- src:27 | Attorney General
-- src:28 | (a) with respect to proceedings to which this Act applies, means the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province in which those proceedings are taken and includes his or her lawful deputy or, if those proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1), the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province in which those proceedings are taken and includes the lawful deputy of any of them,
-- src:29 | (b) means the Attorney General of Canada and includes his or her lawful deputy with respect to
-- src:30 | (i) Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, or
-- src:31 | (ii) proceedings commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government in respect of an offence under any Act of Parliament — other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act — or any regulation made under such an Act, and
-- src:32 | (c) means the Director of Public Prosecutions appointed under subsection 3(1) of the Director of Public Prosecutions Act with respect to proceedings in relation to an offence under the Canada Elections Act; (procureur général)
@ref s 2 "Attorney General" (src:27-32)
DECLARE `s 2 Attorney General: facts of the proceedings` HAS
    `the proceedings are ones to which this Act applies, taken in a province`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- para (a)
    `the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- para (a); the answer of `s 2.3(1) the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)`
    `the proceedings are in Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- para (b)(i)
    `the proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government in respect of an offence under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act, or a regulation made under such an Act`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- para (b)(ii)
    `the proceedings are in relation to an offence under the Canada Elections Act`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- para (c)

@ref s 2 "Attorney General" (src:27-32)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 2 Attorney General: facts of the proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Party)
`s 2 Attorney General` MEANS
    IF NOT (`para (a) applies` OR `para (b) applies` OR `para (c) applies`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) speaks to these proceedings
    ELSE JUST (append `the provincial limb` (append `the federal limb` `the elections limb`))
    WHERE
        `para (a) applies` MEANS facts's `the proceedings are ones to which this Act applies, taken in a province`
        `para (b) applies` MEANS
                facts's `the proceedings are in Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut`
            OR  facts's `the proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government in respect of an offence under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or the Canada Elections Act, or a regulation made under such an Act`
        `para (c) applies` MEANS facts's `the proceedings are in relation to an offence under the Canada Elections Act`
        `the provincial limb` MEANS IF `para (a) applies` THEN LIST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province` ELSE EMPTY
        `the federal limb` MEANS IF (`para (a) applies` AND facts's `the proceedings are referred to in subsection 2.3(1)`) OR `para (b) applies` THEN LIST `the Attorney General of Canada` ELSE EMPTY
        `the elections limb` MEANS IF `para (c) applies` THEN LIST `the Director of Public Prosecutions` ELSE EMPTY

-- audioconference means any means of telecommunication that allows the judge or justice and any individual to communicate orally in a proceeding.
-- src:33 | audioconference means any means of telecommunication that allows the judge or justice and any individual to communicate orally in a proceeding; (audioconférence)
@ref s 2 "audioconference" (src:33)
GIVEN `it is a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it allows the judge or justice and any individual to communicate orally in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 audioconference` MEANS
    IF `it is a means of telecommunication` AND `it allows the judge or justice and any individual to communicate orally in a proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "audioconference means any means of telecommunication that allows the judge or justice and any individual to communicate orally in a proceeding"

-- bank-note includes any negotiable instrument (a) issued by or on behalf of a banker, and (b) issued under lawful authority, intended to be used as money, and includes bank bills and bank post bills.
-- src:34 | bank-note includes any negotiable instrument
-- src:35 | (a) issued by or on behalf of a person carrying on the business of banking in or out of Canada, and
-- src:36 | (b) issued under the authority of Parliament or under the lawful authority of the government of a state other than Canada,
-- src:37 | intended to be used as money or as the equivalent of money, immediately on issue or at some time subsequent thereto, and includes bank bills and bank post bills; (billet de banque)
@ref s 2 "bank-note" (src:34-37)
DECLARE `s 2 bank-note: facts of the instrument` HAS
    `it is a negotiable instrument`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was issued by or on behalf of a person carrying on the business of banking in or out of Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `it was issued under the authority of Parliament or under the lawful authority of the government of a state other than Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it is intended to be used as money or as the equivalent of money, immediately on issue or at some time subsequent thereto`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a bank bill`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a bank post bill`      IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 2 "bank-note" (src:34-37)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 2 bank-note: facts of the instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 bank-note` MEANS
    IF     (    facts's `it is a negotiable instrument`
            AND facts's `it was issued by or on behalf of a person carrying on the business of banking in or out of Canada`
            AND facts's `it was issued under the authority of Parliament or under the lawful authority of the government of a state other than Canada`
            AND facts's `it is intended to be used as money or as the equivalent of money, immediately on issue or at some time subsequent thereto`)
        OR facts's `it is a bank bill`
        OR facts's `it is a bank post bill`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "bank-note includes any negotiable instrument"

-- bodily harm means any hurt or injury to a person that interferes with the health or comfort of the person and that is more than merely transient or trifling in nature.
-- "More than merely transient or trifling" is an open-textured judgement, taken as a plain input.
-- src:38 | bodily harm means any hurt or injury to a person that interferes with the health or comfort of the person and that is more than merely transient or trifling in nature; (lésions corporelles)
@ref s 2 "bodily harm" (src:38)
GIVEN `it is a hurt or injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it interferes with the health or comfort of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is more than merely transient or trifling in nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 bodily harm` MEANS
    IF `it is a hurt or injury to a person` AND `it interferes with the health or comfort of the person` AND `it is more than merely transient or trifling in nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "bodily harm means any hurt or injury to a person that interferes with the health or comfort of the person and that is more than merely transient or trifling in nature"

-- Canadian Forces means the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada.
-- src:39 | Canadian Forces means the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada; (Forces canadiennes)
@ref s 2 "Canadian Forces" (src:39)
GIVEN `they are the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Canadian Forces` MEANS
    IF `they are the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Canadian Forces means the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada"

-- cattle means neat cattle or an animal of the bovine species ..., and includes any horse, mule, ass, pig, sheep or goat.
-- "Means ... and includes ..." is read as closed: an animal that is none of these is not cattle (a marginal reading, see NOTES.md).
-- src:40 | cattle means neat cattle or an animal of the bovine species by whatever technical or familiar name it is known, and includes any horse, mule, ass, pig, sheep or goat; (bétail)
@ref s 2 "cattle" (src:40)
DECLARE `s 2 cattle animal` IS ONE OF
    `neat cattle`
    `an animal of the bovine species by whatever technical or familiar name it is known`
    `a horse`
    `a mule`
    `an ass`
    `a pig`
    `a sheep`
    `a goat`
    `an animal that is none of those named in the definition of cattle`

@ref s 2 "cattle" (src:40)
GIVEN animal IS A `s 2 cattle animal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 cattle` MEANS
    CONSIDER animal
    WHEN `neat cattle` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an animal of the bovine species by whatever technical or familiar name it is known` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a horse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a mule` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an ass` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a pig` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a sheep` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a goat` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an animal that is none of those named in the definition of cattle` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cattle means neat cattle or an animal of the bovine species by whatever technical or familiar name it is known"

-- clerk of the court includes a person, by whatever name or title designated, who from time to time performs the duties of a clerk of the court.
-- src:41 | clerk of the court includes a person, by whatever name or title he may be designated, who from time to time performs the duties of a clerk of the court; (greffier du tribunal)
@ref s 2 "clerk of the court" (src:41)
DECLARE `s 2 clerk of the court kind` IS ONE OF
    `a clerk of the court`
    `a person who, by whatever name or title they are designated, from time to time performs the duties of a clerk of the court`
    `a person who neither is a clerk of the court nor performs a clerk of the court's duties`

@ref s 2 "clerk of the court" (src:41)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 clerk of the court kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 clerk of the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a clerk of the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who, by whatever name or title they are designated, from time to time performs the duties of a clerk of the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who neither is a clerk of the court nor performs a clerk of the court's duties` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "clerk of the court includes"

-- common-law partner, in relation to an individual, means a person who is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year.
-- src:42 | common-law partner, in relation to an individual, means a person who is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year; (conjoint de fait)
@ref s 2 "common-law partner" (src:42)
GIVEN `the person is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months for which the person has so cohabited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 common-law partner` MEANS
    IF `the person is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship` AND `the months for which the person has so cohabited` AT LEAST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year"

-- complainant means the victim of an alleged offence: whatever `s 2 victim` answers.
-- src:43 | complainant means the victim of an alleged offence; (plaignant)
@ref s 2 "complainant" (src:43)
GIVEN `the person is the victim of the alleged offence, by s 2 victim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 complainant` MEANS `the person is the victim of the alleged offence, by s 2 victim`   -- JUST FALSE is the text's own "means"; NOTHING only if s 2 victim is itself not covered

-- counsel means a barrister or solicitor, in respect of the matters or things that barristers and solicitors, respectively, are authorized by the law of a province to do or perform in relation to legal proceedings.
-- src:44 | counsel means a barrister or solicitor, in respect of the matters or things that barristers and solicitors, respectively, are authorized by the law of a province to do or perform in relation to legal proceedings; (avocat)
@ref s 2 "counsel" (src:44)
GIVEN `the person is a barrister or solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one that the law of a province authorizes a barrister or solicitor, respectively, to do or perform in relation to legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 counsel` MEANS
    IF `the person is a barrister or solicitor` AND `the matter is one that the law of a province authorizes a barrister or solicitor, respectively, to do or perform in relation to legal proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "counsel means a barrister or solicitor, in respect of the matters or things"

-- count means a charge in an information or indictment.
-- src:45 | count means a charge in an information or indictment; (chef d’accusation)
@ref s 2 "count" (src:45)
GIVEN `it is a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document it is in` IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 count` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "count means a charge"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the document it is in`
         WHEN `an information` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an indictment` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a charge in an information or indictment"

-- court of appeal means, in all provinces, the Court of Appeal.
-- src:46 | court of appeal means, in all provinces, the Court of Appeal. (cour d’appel)
@ref s 2 "court of appeal" (src:46)
GIVEN `it is the Court of Appeal of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 court of appeal` MEANS
    IF `it is the Court of Appeal of the province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court of appeal means, in all provinces, the Court of Appeal"

-- The named courts of the two court definitions (s 2 "court of criminal jurisdiction" and s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction"),
-- as the text names them, with a member for a court the definitions do not name.
-- src:47 | court of criminal jurisdiction means
-- src:48 | (a) a court of general or quarter sessions of the peace, when presided over by a superior court judge,
-- src:49 | (a.1) in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Quebec, the municipal court of Montreal and the municipal court of Quebec,
-- src:50 | (b) a provincial court judge or judge acting under Part XIX, and
-- src:51 | (c) in the Province of Ontario, the Ontario Court of Justice; (cour de juridiction criminelle)
@ref s 2 "court of criminal jurisdiction" (src:47-51)
DECLARE `s 2 named court` IS ONE OF
    `a court of general or quarter sessions of the peace, presided over by a superior court judge`
    `a court of general or quarter sessions of the peace, not presided over by a superior court judge`
    `the Court of Quebec`
    `the municipal court of Montreal`
    `the municipal court of Quebec`
    `a provincial court judge, or a judge acting under Part XIX`
    `the Ontario Court of Justice`
    `the Court of Appeal`
    `the Superior Court of Justice`
    `the Superior Court`
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    `the Nunavut Court of Justice`
    `a court that none of the two court definitions names`

@ref s 2 "court of criminal jurisdiction" (src:47-51)
GIVEN court IS A `s 2 named court`
      province IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `a court of general or quarter sessions of the peace, presided over by a superior court judge` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
    WHEN `a court of general or quarter sessions of the peace, not presided over by a superior court judge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when presided over by a superior court judge"
    WHEN `the Court of Quebec` THEN `in the Province of Quebec`   -- (a.1)
    WHEN `the municipal court of Montreal` THEN `in the Province of Quebec`
    WHEN `the municipal court of Quebec` THEN `in the Province of Quebec`
    WHEN `a provincial court judge, or a judge acting under Part XIX` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
    WHEN `the Ontario Court of Justice` THEN IF province EQUALS Ontario THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- (c); FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the Province of Ontario, the Ontario Court of Justice"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court of criminal jurisdiction means"
    WHERE
        `in the Province of Quebec` MEANS
            IF province EQUALS Quebec
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Quebec, the municipal court of Montreal and the municipal court of Quebec"

-- superior court of criminal jurisdiction means (a) Ontario: the Court of Appeal or the Superior Court of Justice; (b) Quebec: the Superior Court; (c) Nova Scotia, British Columbia,
-- Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador: the Court of Appeal or the Supreme Court; (d) New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta: the Court of Appeal or the Court of Queen’s Bench;
-- (e) Yukon and the Northwest Territories: the Supreme Court; (f) Nunavut: the Nunavut Court of Justice. (g) and (h) are repealed (line 189). Paragraph (b) does not name the Court of Appeal of Quebec: encoded as the text has it.
-- src:182 | superior court of criminal jurisdiction means
-- src:183 | (a) in the Province of Ontario, the Court of Appeal or the Superior Court of Justice,
-- src:184 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, the Superior Court,
-- src:185 | (c) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, the Court of Appeal or the Supreme Court,
-- src:186 | (d) in the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Court of Appeal or the Court of Queen’s Bench,
-- src:187 | (e) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, the Supreme Court, and
-- src:188 | (f) in Nunavut, the Nunavut Court of Justice; (cour supérieure de juridiction criminelle)
@ref s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" (src:182-188)
GIVEN court IS A `s 2 named court`
      province IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF province EQUALS Ontario AND (court EQUALS `the Court of Appeal` OR court EQUALS `the Superior Court of Justice`) THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF province EQUALS Quebec AND court EQUALS `the Superior Court` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
        IF `in a province named in paragraph (c)` AND (court EQUALS `the Court of Appeal` OR court EQUALS `the Supreme Court`) THEN JUST TRUE   -- (c)
        IF `in a province named in paragraph (d)` AND (court EQUALS `the Court of Appeal` OR court EQUALS `the Court of Queen’s Bench`) THEN JUST TRUE   -- (d)
        IF (province EQUALS Yukon OR province EQUALS `Northwest Territories`) AND court EQUALS `the Supreme Court` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (e)
        IF province EQUALS Nunavut AND court EQUALS `the Nunavut Court of Justice` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (f)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "superior court of criminal jurisdiction means"
    WHERE
        `in a province named in paragraph (c)` MEANS
            province EQUALS `Nova Scotia` OR province EQUALS `British Columbia` OR province EQUALS `Prince Edward Island` OR province EQUALS `Newfoundland and Labrador`
        `in a province named in paragraph (d)` MEANS
            province EQUALS `New Brunswick` OR province EQUALS Manitoba OR province EQUALS Saskatchewan OR province EQUALS Alberta

-- (g) and (h) of "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" are shown repealed: no operative text. Carried as a quotation only.
-- src:189 | (g) and (h) [Repealed, 2015, c. 3, s. 44]
@ref s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" paragraphs (g) and (h), repealed (src:189)
`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction paragraphs (g) and (h) as the text shows them` MEANS "(g) and (h) [Repealed, 2015, c. 3, s. 44]"

-- criminal organization has the same meaning as in subsection 467.1(1): the definition is in another part. Its answer is taken as an input, named for that section.
-- src:52 | criminal organization has the same meaning as in subsection 467.1(1); (organisation criminelle)
@ref s 2 "criminal organization" (src:52)
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 criminal organization` MEANS `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)`

-- The forms in which a charge can touch an offence named in a definition (criminal organization offence para (b), terrorism offence para (d)).
-- src:53 | criminal organization offence means
-- src:54 | (a) an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a serious offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, or
-- src:55 | (b) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in paragraph (a); (infraction d’organisation criminelle)
@ref s 2 "criminal organization offence" (src:53-55)
DECLARE `s 2 form of the charge` IS ONE OF
    `the offence itself`
    `a conspiracy to commit the offence`
    `an attempt to commit the offence`
    `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence`
    `counselling in relation to the offence`
    `a form of participation that is none of those`

-- criminal organization offence means (a) an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a serious offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization,
-- or (b) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref s 2 "criminal organization offence" (src:53-55)
GIVEN form IS A `s 2 form of the charge`
      `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence is a serious offence, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 criminal organization offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `the offence itself` THEN `paragraph (a) holds`
    WHEN `a conspiracy to commit the offence` THEN `paragraph (a) holds`   -- (b)
    WHEN `an attempt to commit the offence` THEN `paragraph (a) holds`
    WHEN `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence` THEN `paragraph (a) holds`
    WHEN `counselling in relation to the offence` THEN `paragraph (a) holds`
    WHEN `a form of participation that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "criminal organization offence means"
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS
            IF `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns`'s `section` EQUALS 467.11
                OR `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns`'s `section` EQUALS 467.111
                OR `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns`'s `section` EQUALS 467.12
                OR `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns`'s `section` EQUALS 467.13
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE IF NOT `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`
                 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a serious offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization"
                 ELSE `the offence is a serious offence, by s 467.1(1)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("means"); NOTHING when s 467.1(1) is itself not covered

-- day means the period between six o’clock in the forenoon and nine o’clock in the afternoon of the same day. The time of day is given in minutes after midnight
-- (6:00 is 360, 21:00 is 1260). FORK: "between" does not say whether the end-points belong to "day" or to "night" (the definition of night uses "between" for the same two instants): NOTHING at 360 and 1260.
-- src:56 | day means the period between six o’clock in the forenoon and nine o’clock in the afternoon of the same day; (jour)
@ref s 2 "day" (src:56)
GIVEN `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` LESS THAN 0 OR `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` AT LEAST 1440 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not a time of day
        IF `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS 360 OR `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS 1260 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "between six o’clock in the forenoon and nine o’clock in the afternoon" does not say whether the end-points are in
        IF `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` GREATER THAN 360 AND `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` LESS THAN 1260 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "day means the period between six o’clock in the forenoon and nine o’clock in the afternoon of the same day"

-- document of title to goods includes a bought and sold note, bill of lading, warrant, certificate or order for the delivery or transfer of goods ..., and any other document used in the ordinary course of business as evidence of possession or control of goods ...
-- src:57 | document of title to goods includes a bought and sold note, bill of lading, warrant, certificate or order for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing, and any other document used in the ordinary course of business as evidence of the possession or control of goods, authorizing or purporting to authorize, by endorsement or by delivery, the person in possession of the document to transfer or receive any goods thereby represented or therein mentioned or referred to; (titre de marchandises)
@ref s 2 "document of title to goods" (src:57)
DECLARE `s 2 document of title to goods kind` IS ONE OF
    `a bought and sold note`
    `a bill of lading`
    `a warrant for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing`
    `a certificate for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing`
    `an order for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing`
    `any other document used in the ordinary course of business as evidence of the possession or control of goods, authorizing or purporting to authorize, by endorsement or by delivery, the person in possession of the document to transfer or receive any goods thereby represented or therein mentioned or referred to`
    `a document that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "document of title to goods" (src:57)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 document of title to goods kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 document of title to goods` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a bought and sold note` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a bill of lading` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a warrant for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a certificate for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an order for the delivery or transfer of goods or any other valuable thing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other document used in the ordinary course of business as evidence of the possession or control of goods, authorizing or purporting to authorize, by endorsement or by delivery, the person in possession of the document to transfer or receive any goods thereby represented or therein mentioned or referred to` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "document of title to goods includes"

-- document of title to lands includes any writing that is or contains evidence of the title ..., any notarial or registrar’s copy, and any duplicate instrument, memorial, certificate or document authorized or required by law with respect to registration of titles.
-- src:58 | document of title to lands includes any writing that is or contains evidence of the title, or any part of the title, to real property or to any interest in real property, and any notarial or registrar’s copy thereof and any duplicate instrument, memorial, certificate or document authorized or required by any law in force in any part of Canada with respect to registration of titles that relates to title to real property or to any interest in real property; (titre de bien-fonds)
@ref s 2 "document of title to lands" (src:58)
DECLARE `s 2 document of title to lands kind` IS ONE OF
    `a writing that is or contains evidence of the title, or any part of the title, to real property or to any interest in real property`
    `a notarial or registrar’s copy of such a writing`
    `a duplicate instrument, memorial, certificate or document authorized or required by any law in force in any part of Canada with respect to registration of titles that relates to title to real property or to any interest in real property`
    `a document that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "document of title to lands" (src:58)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 document of title to lands kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 document of title to lands` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a writing that is or contains evidence of the title, or any part of the title, to real property or to any interest in real property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a notarial or registrar’s copy of such a writing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a duplicate instrument, memorial, certificate or document authorized or required by any law in force in any part of Canada with respect to registration of titles that relates to title to real property or to any interest in real property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "document of title to lands includes"

-- dwelling-house means the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence, and includes (a) a building within the curtilage connected by a doorway or covered and enclosed passage-way,
-- and (b) a mobile unit designed to be used as a residence and that is being used as such. "Means ... and includes" read as closed; a mobile unit not being used as a residence is outside (b)'s own words.
-- src:59 | dwelling-house means the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence, and includes
-- src:60 | (a) a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passage-way, and
-- src:61 | (b) a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence; (maison d’habitation)
@ref s 2 "dwelling-house" (src:59-61)
DECLARE `s 2 dwelling-house kind` IS ONE OF
    `the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence`
    `a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passage-way`   -- (a)
    `a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence`   -- (b)
    `a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is not being used as such a residence`
    `a place that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "dwelling-house" (src:59-61)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 dwelling-house kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 dwelling-house` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passage-way` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is not being used as such a residence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence"
    WHEN `a place that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "dwelling-house means the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence"

-- environment means the components of the Earth and includes (a) air, land and water, (b) all layers of the atmosphere, (c) all organic and inorganic matter and living organisms, and (d) the interacting natural systems ... ("means ... and includes": read as closed).
-- src:62 | environment means the components of the Earth and includes
-- src:63 | (a) air, land and water,
-- src:64 | (b) all layers of the atmosphere,
-- src:65 | (c) all organic and inorganic matter and living organisms, and
-- src:66 | (d) the interacting natural systems that include components referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c); (environnement)
@ref s 2 "environment" (src:62-66)
DECLARE `s 2 environment kind` IS ONE OF
    `a component of the Earth`
    `air, land or water`   -- (a)
    `a layer of the atmosphere`   -- (b)
    `organic or inorganic matter, or a living organism`   -- (c)
    `an interacting natural system that includes components referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c)`   -- (d)
    `a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "environment" (src:62-66)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 environment kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 environment` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a component of the Earth` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `air, land or water` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a layer of the atmosphere` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `organic or inorganic matter, or a living organism` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an interacting natural system that includes components referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "environment means the components of the Earth"

-- every one, person and owner, and similar expressions, include Her Majesty and an organization.
-- src:67 | every one, person and owner, and similar expressions, include Her Majesty and an organization; (quiconque, individu, personne et propriétaire)
@ref s 2 "every one", "person" and "owner" (src:67)
DECLARE `s 2 every one: the expression used` IS ONE OF
    `every one`
    `person`
    `owner`
    `an expression similar to every one, person or owner`
    `an expression that is not similar to those`

DECLARE `s 2 every one: the subject` IS ONE OF
    `Her Majesty`
    `an organization`
    `an individual`
    `a subject of another kind`

@ref s 2 "every one", "person" and "owner" (src:67)
GIVEN expression IS A `s 2 every one: the expression used`
      subject IS A `s 2 every one: the subject`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 every one, person and owner` MEANS
    IF expression EQUALS `an expression that is not similar to those`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the definition reaches "every one, person and owner, and similar expressions" only
    ELSE CONSIDER subject
         WHEN `Her Majesty` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an organization` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an individual` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the definition says what the expressions include, not that an individual is within or outside them
         WHEN `a subject of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include Her Majesty and an organization"

-- explosive substance includes (a) anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance, (b) anything ... used or intended to be used, or adapted to cause, or to aid in causing an explosion in or with an explosive substance, and (c) an incendiary grenade, fire bomb, molotov cocktail ...
-- src:68 | explosive substance includes
-- src:69 | (a) anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance,
-- src:70 | (b) anything, or any part thereof, used or intended to be used, or adapted to cause, or to aid in causing an explosion in or with an explosive substance, and
-- src:71 | (c) an incendiary grenade, fire bomb, molotov cocktail or other similar incendiary substance or device and a delaying mechanism or other thing intended for use in connection with such a substance or device; (substance explosive)
@ref s 2 "explosive substance" (src:68-71)
DECLARE `s 2 explosive substance kind` IS ONE OF
    `anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance`   -- (a)
    `anything, or any part thereof, used or intended to be used, or adapted to cause, or to aid in causing an explosion in or with an explosive substance`   -- (b)
    `an incendiary grenade, fire bomb, molotov cocktail or other similar incendiary substance or device`   -- (c)
    `a delaying mechanism or other thing intended for use in connection with such a substance or device`   -- (c)
    `a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "explosive substance" (src:68-71)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 explosive substance` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `anything intended to be used to make an explosive substance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `anything, or any part thereof, used or intended to be used, or adapted to cause, or to aid in causing an explosion in or with an explosive substance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an incendiary grenade, fire bomb, molotov cocktail or other similar incendiary substance or device` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a delaying mechanism or other thing intended for use in connection with such a substance or device` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "explosive substance includes"

-- feeble-minded person [Repealed]: the text shows no operative words.
-- src:72 | feeble-minded person [Repealed, 1991, c. 43, s. 9]
@ref s 2 "feeble-minded person", repealed (src:72)
`s 2 feeble-minded person as the text shows it` MEANS "feeble-minded person [Repealed, 1991, c. 43, s. 9]"

-- firearm means a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person,
-- and includes any frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon and anything that can be adapted for use as a firearm. ("Means ... and includes": read as closed.)
-- src:73 | firearm means a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person, and includes any frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon and anything that can be adapted for use as a firearm; (arme à feu)
@ref s 2 "firearm" (src:73)
GIVEN `it is a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be adapted for use as a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 firearm` MEANS
    IF     (`it is a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged` AND `it is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person`)
        OR `it is a frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon`
        OR `it can be adapted for use as a firearm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "firearm means a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person"

-- government or public facility means a facility or conveyance, whether permanent or temporary, that is used or occupied in connection with their official duties by [the persons listed].
-- src:74 | government or public facility means a facility or conveyance, whether permanent or temporary, that is used or occupied in connection with their official duties by representatives of a state, members of a government, members of a legislature, members of the judiciary, or officials or employees of a state or of any other public authority or public entity, or by officials or employees of an intergovernmental organization; (installation gouvernementale ou publique)
@ref s 2 "government or public facility" (src:74)
DECLARE `s 2 government or public facility: who uses it` IS ONE OF
    `representatives of a state`
    `members of a government`
    `members of a legislature`
    `members of the judiciary`
    `officials or employees of a state or of any other public authority or public entity`
    `officials or employees of an intergovernmental organization`
    `users who are none of those`

@ref s 2 "government or public facility" (src:74)
GIVEN `it is a facility or conveyance, whether permanent or temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
      users IS A `s 2 government or public facility: who uses it`
      `it is used or occupied in connection with their official duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 government or public facility` MEANS
    IF `it is a facility or conveyance, whether permanent or temporary` AND `it is used or occupied in connection with their official duties` AND NOT (users EQUALS `users who are none of those`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "government or public facility means a facility or conveyance, whether permanent or temporary, that is used or occupied in connection with their official duties"

-- Her Majesty’s Forces means the naval, army and air forces of Her Majesty wherever raised, and includes the Canadian Forces.
-- src:75 | Her Majesty’s Forces means the naval, army and air forces of Her Majesty wherever raised, and includes the Canadian Forces; (forces de Sa Majesté)
@ref s 2 "Her Majesty’s Forces" (src:75)
DECLARE `s 2 Her Majesty’s Forces kind` IS ONE OF
    `the naval, army and air forces of Her Majesty wherever raised`
    `the Canadian Forces`
    `forces that are neither of those`

@ref s 2 "Her Majesty’s Forces" (src:75)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 Her Majesty’s Forces kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Her Majesty’s Forces` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the naval, army and air forces of Her Majesty wherever raised` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Canadian Forces` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forces that are neither of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Her Majesty’s Forces means the naval, army and air forces of Her Majesty wherever raised"

-- highway means a road to which the public has the right of access, and includes bridges over which or tunnels through which a road passes.
-- src:76 | highway means a road to which the public has the right of access, and includes bridges over which or tunnels through which a road passes; (voie publique ou grande route)
