    `a road to which the public has the right of access`
    `a bridge over which a road passes`
    `a tunnel through which a road passes`
    `a road to which the public has no right of access`
    `a way that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "highway" (src:76)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 highway kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 highway` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a road to which the public has the right of access` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a bridge over which a road passes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a tunnel through which a road passes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a road to which the public has no right of access` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "highway means a road to which the public has the right of access"
    WHEN `a way that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "highway means a road to which the public has the right of access"

-- indictment includes (a) information or a count therein, (b) a plea, replication or other pleading, and (c) any record.
