    `an information, or a count in an information`   -- (a)
    `a plea, replication or other pleading`   -- (b)
    `any record`   -- (c)
    `a document that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "indictment" (src:77-80)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 indictment kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 indictment` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an information, or a count in an information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a plea, replication or other pleading` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any record` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "indictment includes"

-- internationally protected person means (a) a head of state ... whenever in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position; (b) a family member who accompanies that person in such a state;
-- (c) a representative or an official of a state or an official or agent of an international organization of an intergovernmental character who, at the time and place of an offence referred to in subsection 7(3) ..., is entitled, pursuant to international law, to special protection; (d) a family member who forms part of that person's household, on the same condition.
-- src:81 | internationally protected person means
-- src:82 | (a) a head of state, including any member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, whenever that person is in a state other than the state in which he holds that position or office,
-- src:83 | (b) a member of the family of a person described in paragraph (a) who accompanies that person in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office,
-- src:84 | (c) a representative or an official of a state or an official or agent of an international organization of an intergovernmental character who, at the time when and at the place where an offence referred to in subsection 7(3) is committed against his person or any property referred to in section 431 that is used by him, is entitled, pursuant to international law, to special protection from any attack on his person, freedom or dignity, or
-- src:85 | (d) a member of the family of a representative, official or agent described in paragraph (c) who forms part of his household, if the representative, official or agent, at the time when and at the place where any offence referred to in subsection 7(3) is committed against the member of his family or any property referred to in section 431 that is used by that member, is entitled, pursuant to international law, to special protection from any attack on his person, freedom or dignity; (personne jouissant d’une protection internationale)
@ref s 2 "internationally protected person" (src:81-85)
DECLARE `s 2 internationally protected person basis` IS ONE OF
    `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office`   -- (a)
    `a head of state, head of a government or minister of foreign affairs, while in the state in which that person holds that position or office`
    `a member of the family of a person described in paragraph (a) who accompanies that person in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office`   -- (b)
    `a member of the family of a person described in paragraph (a) who does not accompany that person in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office`
    `a representative or an official of a state or an official or agent of an international organization of an intergovernmental character`   -- (c)
    `a member of the family of a representative, official or agent described in paragraph (c) who forms part of their household`   -- (d)
    `a person who is none of those`

@ref s 2 "internationally protected person" (src:81-85)
GIVEN basis IS A `s 2 internationally protected person basis`
      `at the time and place of an offence referred to in subsection 7(3) against the person or property referred to in section 431 used by them, the representative, official or agent is entitled, pursuant to international law, to special protection from any attack on their person, freedom or dignity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 internationally protected person` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `a head of state, including a member of a collegial body that performs the functions of a head of state under the constitution of the state concerned, a head of a government or a minister of foreign affairs, while in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a head of state, head of a government or minister of foreign affairs, while in the state in which that person holds that position or office` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whenever that person is in a state other than the state in which he holds that position or office"
    WHEN `a member of the family of a person described in paragraph (a) who accompanies that person in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the family of a person described in paragraph (a) who does not accompany that person in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who accompanies that person in a state other than the state in which that person holds that position or office"
    WHEN `a representative or an official of a state or an official or agent of an international organization of an intergovernmental character` THEN `the entitlement limb`
    WHEN `a member of the family of a representative, official or agent described in paragraph (c) who forms part of their household` THEN `the entitlement limb`
    WHEN `a person who is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "internationally protected person means"
    WHERE
        `the entitlement limb` MEANS
            IF `at the time and place of an offence referred to in subsection 7(3) against the person or property referred to in section 431 used by them, the representative, official or agent is entitled, pursuant to international law, to special protection from any attack on their person, freedom or dignity`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled, pursuant to international law, to special protection from any attack on his person, freedom or dignity"

-- intimate partner with respect to a person, includes their current or former spouse, common-law partner and dating partner.
-- src:86 | intimate partner with respect to a person, includes their current or former spouse, common-law partner and dating partner; (partenaire intime)
