    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `a current spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a former spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a current common-law partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a former common-law partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a current dating partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a former dating partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person in some other relationship to the person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "intimate partner with respect to a person, includes"

-- justice means a justice of the peace or a provincial court judge, and includes two or more justices where two or more justices are, by law, required to act or, by law, act or have jurisdiction.
-- src:87 | justice means a justice of the peace or a provincial court judge, and includes two or more justices where two or more justices are, by law, required to act or, by law, act or have jurisdiction; (juge de paix)
