DECLARE `s 2 justice kind` IS ONE OF
    `a justice of the peace`
    `a provincial court judge as the definition of justice names them`
    `two or more justices, where two or more justices are, by law, required to act`
    `two or more justices, where two or more justices by law act or have jurisdiction`
    `a judicial officer who is none of those`

@ref s 2 "justice" (src:87)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 justice kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a justice of the peace` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a provincial court judge as the definition of justice names them` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `two or more justices, where two or more justices are, by law, required to act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `two or more justices, where two or more justices by law act or have jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a judicial officer who is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "justice means a justice of the peace or a provincial court judge"

-- justice system participant means (a) a member of the Senate, House of Commons, legislative assembly or municipal council, (b) a person who plays a role in the administration of criminal justice, including (i) to (xi), and (c) a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving (i) to (v).
-- src:88 | justice system participant means
-- src:89 | (a) a member of the Senate, of the House of Commons, of a legislative assembly or of a municipal council,
-- src:90 | (b) a person who plays a role in the administration of criminal justice, including
-- src:91 | (i) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness and a Minister responsible for policing in a province,
-- src:92 | (ii) a prosecutor, a lawyer, a member of the Chambre des notaires du Québec and an officer of a court,
-- src:93 | (iii) a judge and a justice,
-- src:94 | (iv) a juror and a person who is summoned as a juror,
-- src:95 | (v) an informant, a prospective witness, a witness under subpoena and a witness who has testified,
-- src:96 | (vi) a peace officer within the meaning of any of paragraphs (b), (c), (d), (e) and (g) of the definition peace officer,
-- src:97 | (vii) a civilian employee of a police force,
-- src:98 | (viii) a person employed in the administration of a court,
-- src:99 | (viii.1) a public officer within the meaning of subsection 25.1(1) and a person acting at the direction of such an officer,
-- src:100 | (ix) an employee of the Canada Revenue Agency who is involved in the investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament,
-- src:101 | (ix.1) an employee of the Canada Border Services Agency who is involved in the investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament,
-- src:102 | (x) an employee of a federal or provincial correctional service, a parole supervisor and any other person who is involved in the administration of a sentence under the supervision of such a correctional service and a person who conducts disciplinary hearings under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, and
-- src:103 | (xi) an employee and a member of the Parole Board of Canada and of a provincial parole board, and
-- src:104 | (c) a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving
-- src:105 | (i) security information,
-- src:106 | (ii) criminal intelligence information,
-- src:107 | (iii) information that would endanger the safety of any person if it were disclosed,
-- src:108 | (iv) information that is obtained in confidence from a source in Canada, the government of a foreign state, an international organization of states or an institution of such a government or international organization, or
-- src:109 | (v) potentially injurious information or sensitive information as those terms are defined in section 38 of the Canada Evidence Act; (personne associée au système judiciaire)
@ref s 2 "justice system participant" (src:88-109)
DECLARE `s 2 justice system participant role` IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Senate, of the House of Commons, of a legislative assembly or of a municipal council`   -- (a)
    `a person who plays a role in the administration of criminal justice and is not named in (b)(i) to (xi)`   -- (b)
    `the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or a Minister responsible for policing in a province`   -- (b)(i)
    `a prosecutor, a lawyer, a member of the Chambre des notaires du Québec or an officer of a court`   -- (b)(ii)
    `a judge or a justice`   -- (b)(iii)
    `a juror or a person who is summoned as a juror`   -- (b)(iv)
    `an informant, a prospective witness, a witness under subpoena or a witness who has testified`   -- (b)(v)
    `a peace officer within the meaning of any of paragraphs (b), (c), (d), (e) and (g) of the definition peace officer`   -- (b)(vi)
    `a civilian employee of a police force`   -- (b)(vii)
    `a person employed in the administration of a court`   -- (b)(viii)
    `a public officer within the meaning of subsection 25.1(1) or a person acting at the direction of such an officer`   -- (b)(viii.1)
    `an employee of the Canada Revenue Agency who is involved in the investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament`   -- (b)(ix)
    `an employee of the Canada Border Services Agency who is involved in the investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament`   -- (b)(ix.1)
    `an employee of a federal or provincial correctional service, a parole supervisor, any other person who is involved in the administration of a sentence under the supervision of such a correctional service, or a person who conducts disciplinary hearings under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`   -- (b)(x)
    `an employee or a member of the Parole Board of Canada or of a provincial parole board`   -- (b)(xi)
    `a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving security information`   -- (c)(i)
    `a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving criminal intelligence information`   -- (c)(ii)
    `a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving information that would endanger the safety of any person if it were disclosed`   -- (c)(iii)
    `a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving information that is obtained in confidence from a source in Canada, the government of a foreign state, an international organization of states or an institution of such a government or international organization`   -- (c)(iv)
    `a person who plays a role in respect of proceedings involving potentially injurious information or sensitive information as those terms are defined in section 38 of the Canada Evidence Act`   -- (c)(v)
    `a person who is none of those`

@ref s 2 "justice system participant" (src:88-109)
GIVEN role IS A `s 2 justice system participant role`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 justice system participant` MEANS
    CONSIDER role
    WHEN `a person who is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "justice system participant means"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- every other role is named in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)

