    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "mental disorder means a disease of the mind"

-- military shall be construed as relating to all or any of the Canadian Forces. A rule of construction, not a "means": what the word does not relate to is not said (NOTHING).
-- src:112 | military shall be construed as relating to all or any of the Canadian Forces; (militaire)
@ref s 2 "military" (src:112)
DECLARE `s 2 military: what the word relates to` IS ONE OF
    `all of the Canadian Forces`
    `any of the Canadian Forces`
    `something other than the Canadian Forces`

@ref s 2 "military" (src:112)
GIVEN `what the word is said to relate to` IS A `s 2 military: what the word relates to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 military` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the word is said to relate to`
    WHEN `all of the Canadian Forces` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any of the Canadian Forces` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something other than the Canadian Forces` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what "military" shall be construed as relating to, not that it relates to nothing else

-- military law includes all laws, regulations or orders relating to the Canadian Forces.
-- src:113 | military law includes all laws, regulations or orders relating to the Canadian Forces; (loi militaire)
@ref s 2 "military law" (src:113)
DECLARE `s 2 military law kind` IS ONE OF
    `a law relating to the Canadian Forces`
    `a regulation relating to the Canadian Forces`
    `an order relating to the Canadian Forces`
    `an instrument that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "military law" (src:113)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 military law kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 military law` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a law relating to the Canadian Forces` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a regulation relating to the Canadian Forces` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an order relating to the Canadian Forces` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "military law includes"

-- motor vehicle means a vehicle that is drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power, but does not include railway equipment.
-- src:114 | motor vehicle means a vehicle that is drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power, but does not include railway equipment; (véhicule à moteur)
@ref s 2 "motor vehicle" (src:114)
GIVEN `it is a vehicle that is drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is railway equipment, by s 2 railway equipment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 motor vehicle` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a vehicle that is drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "motor vehicle means a vehicle that is drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power"
    ELSE CONSIDER `it is railway equipment, by s 2 railway equipment`
         WHEN JUST isRailwayEquipment THEN IF isRailwayEquipment THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include railway equipment"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether it is railway equipment is not determined

-- municipality includes the corporation of a city, town, village, county, township, parish or other territorial or local division of a province, the inhabitants of which are incorporated or are entitled to hold property collectively for a public purpose.
-- src:115 | municipality includes the corporation of a city, town, village, county, township, parish or other territorial or local division of a province, the inhabitants of which are incorporated or are entitled to hold property collectively for a public purpose; (municipalité)
@ref s 2 "municipality" (src:115)
DECLARE `s 2 municipality: the division` IS ONE OF
    `a city`
    `a town`
    `a village`
    `a county`
    `a township`
    `a parish`
    `another territorial or local division of a province`
    `a body that is not a territorial or local division of a province`

@ref s 2 "municipality" (src:115)
GIVEN division IS A `s 2 municipality: the division`
      `its inhabitants are incorporated or are entitled to hold property collectively for a public purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 municipality` MEANS
    IF division EQUALS `a body that is not a territorial or local division of a province`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "municipality includes the corporation of a city, town, village, county, township, parish or other territorial or local division of a province"
    ELSE IF `its inhabitants are incorporated or are entitled to hold property collectively for a public purpose`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the list is introduced by "includes", so a division whose inhabitants are neither incorporated nor entitled to hold property collectively is outside this limb, not outside the term

-- newly-born child means a person under the age of one year (the age is given in years).
-- src:116 | newly-born child means a person under the age of one year; (enfant nouveau-né ou nouveau-né)
@ref s 2 "newly-born child" (src:116)
GIVEN `the age of the person, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 newly-born child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the age of the person, in years` LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not an age
        IF `the age of the person, in years` LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "newly-born child means a person under the age of one year"

-- night means the period between nine o’clock in the afternoon and six o’clock in the forenoon of the following day (minutes after midnight; the end-points 1260 and 360 are the same fork as in `s 2 day`).
-- src:117 | night means the period between nine o’clock in the afternoon and six o’clock in the forenoon of the following day; (nuit)
@ref s 2 "night" (src:117)
GIVEN `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 night` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` LESS THAN 0 OR `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` AT LEAST 1440 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not a time of day
        IF `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS 360 OR `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS 1260 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "between nine o’clock in the afternoon and six o’clock in the forenoon" does not say whether the end-points are in
        IF `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` GREATER THAN 1260 OR `the time of day, in minutes after midnight` LESS THAN 360 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "night means the period between nine o’clock in the afternoon and six o’clock in the forenoon of the following day"

-- nuclear facility means (a) any nuclear reactor ... and (b) any plant or conveyance used for the production, storage, processing or transport of nuclear material or radioactive material.
-- src:118 | nuclear facility means
-- src:119 | (a) any nuclear reactor, including a reactor installed on a vessel, vehicle, aircraft or space object for use as an energy source in order to propel the vessel, vehicle, aircraft or space object or for any other purpose, and
-- src:120 | (b) any plant or conveyance used for the production, storage, processing or transport of nuclear material or radioactive material; (installation nucléaire)
@ref s 2 "nuclear facility" (src:118-120)
DECLARE `s 2 nuclear facility kind` IS ONE OF
    `a nuclear reactor, including a reactor installed on a vessel, vehicle, aircraft or space object for use as an energy source in order to propel the vessel, vehicle, aircraft or space object or for any other purpose`   -- (a)
    `a plant or conveyance used for the production, storage, processing or transport of nuclear material or radioactive material`   -- (b)
    `a thing that is neither of those`

@ref s 2 "nuclear facility" (src:118-120)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 nuclear facility kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 nuclear facility` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a nuclear reactor, including a reactor installed on a vessel, vehicle, aircraft or space object for use as an energy source in order to propel the vessel, vehicle, aircraft or space object or for any other purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a plant or conveyance used for the production, storage, processing or transport of nuclear material or radioactive material` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing that is neither of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nuclear facility means"

-- nuclear material means (a) plutonium, except plutonium with an isotopic concentration of plutonium-238 that is greater than 80%; (b) uranium-233; (c) uranium containing uranium-233 or uranium-235 or both in an amount such that the abundance ratio of
-- the sum of those isotopes to the isotope uranium-238 is greater than 0.72%; (d) uranium with an isotopic concentration equal to that occurring in nature, except uranium in the form of ore or ore-residue; (e) any substance containing any material described in (a) to (d).
-- src:121 | nuclear material means
-- src:122 | (a) plutonium, except plutonium with an isotopic concentration of plutonium-238 that is greater than 80%,
-- src:123 | (b) uranium-233,
-- src:124 | (c) uranium containing uranium-233 or uranium-235 or both in an amount such that the abundance ratio of the sum of those isotopes to the isotope uranium-238 is greater than 0.72%,
-- src:125 | (d) uranium with an isotopic concentration equal to that occurring in nature, except uranium in the form of ore or ore-residue, and
-- src:126 | (e) any substance containing any material described in paragraphs (a) to (d); (matière nucléaire)
@ref s 2 "nuclear material" (src:121-126)
DECLARE `s 2 nuclear material: the substance` IS ONE OF
    `plutonium`   -- (a)
    `uranium-233`   -- (b)
    `uranium containing uranium-233 or uranium-235 or both`   -- (c)
    `uranium with an isotopic concentration equal to that occurring in nature`   -- (d)
    `any substance containing any material described in paragraphs (a) to (d)`   -- (e)
    `a substance that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "nuclear material" (src:121-126)
GIVEN substance IS A `s 2 nuclear material: the substance`
      `the isotopic concentration of plutonium-238, in percent` IS A NUMBER   -- read for plutonium only
      `the abundance ratio of the sum of uranium-233 and uranium-235 to uranium-238, in percent` IS A NUMBER   -- read for (c) only
      `the uranium is in the form of ore or ore-residue` IS A BOOLEAN   -- read for (d) only
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 nuclear material` MEANS
    CONSIDER substance
    WHEN `plutonium` THEN IF `the isotopic concentration of plutonium-238, in percent` GREATER THAN 80 THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except plutonium with an isotopic concentration of plutonium-238 that is greater than 80%"
    WHEN `uranium-233` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `uranium containing uranium-233 or uranium-235 or both` THEN IF `the abundance ratio of the sum of uranium-233 and uranium-235 to uranium-238, in percent` GREATER THAN 0.72 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is greater than 0.72%" (a ratio of 0.72% or less is outside (c); uranium at the natural concentration is (d))
    WHEN `uranium with an isotopic concentration equal to that occurring in nature` THEN IF `the uranium is in the form of ore or ore-residue` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except uranium in the form of ore or ore-residue"
    WHEN `any substance containing any material described in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a substance that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nuclear material means"

-- offence-related property means any property, within or outside Canada, (a) by means or in respect of which an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act is committed, (b) that is used in any manner in connection with the commission of such an offence, or (c) that is intended to be used for committing such an offence.
-- src:127 | offence-related property means any property, within or outside Canada,
-- src:128 | (a) by means or in respect of which an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act is committed,
-- src:129 | (b) that is used in any manner in connection with the commission of such an offence, or
-- src:130 | (c) that is intended to be used for committing such an offence; (bien infractionnel)
@ref s 2 "offence-related property" (src:127-130)
GIVEN `it is property, by s 2 property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act is committed by means or in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it is used in any manner in connection with the commission of such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it is intended to be used for committing such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 offence-related property` MEANS
    IF `an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act is committed by means or in respect of it`
        OR `it is used in any manner in connection with the commission of such an offence`
        OR `it is intended to be used for committing such an offence`
    THEN `it is property, by s 2 property`   -- JUST TRUE when it is property; JUST FALSE ("means any property"); NOTHING when s 2 property leaves it open
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "offence-related property means any property, within or outside Canada, (a) by means or in respect of which an indictable offence under this Act or the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act is committed"

-- offender means a person who has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence, whether on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt.
-- src:131 | offender means a person who has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence, whether on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt; (contrevenant)
@ref s 2 "offender" (src:131)
DECLARE `s 2 offender: how the person stands` IS ONE OF
    `determined by a court to be guilty of an offence on acceptance of a plea of guilty`
    `determined by a court to be guilty of an offence on a finding of guilt`
    `not determined by a court to be guilty of an offence`

@ref s 2 "offender" (src:131)
GIVEN `how the person stands` IS A `s 2 offender: how the person stands`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 offender` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person stands`
    WHEN `determined by a court to be guilty of an offence on acceptance of a plea of guilty` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `determined by a court to be guilty of an offence on a finding of guilt` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `not determined by a court to be guilty of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "offender means a person who has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence"

-- offensive weapon has the same meaning as weapon.
-- src:132 | offensive weapon has the same meaning as weapon; (arme offensive)
@ref s 2 "offensive weapon" (src:132)
GIVEN `it is a weapon, by s 2 weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 offensive weapon` MEANS `it is a weapon, by s 2 weapon`

-- organization means (a) a public body, body corporate, society, company, firm, partnership, trade union or municipality, or (b) an association of persons that (i) is created for a common purpose, (ii) has an operational structure, and (iii) holds itself out to the public as an association of persons.
-- src:133 | organization means
-- src:134 | (a) a public body, body corporate, society, company, firm, partnership, trade union or municipality, or
-- src:135 | (b) an association of persons that
-- src:136 | (i) is created for a common purpose,
-- src:137 | (ii) has an operational structure, and
-- src:138 | (iii) holds itself out to the public as an association of persons; (organisation)
@ref s 2 "organization" (src:133-138)
DECLARE `s 2 organization: the kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `a public body`   -- (a)
    `a body corporate`
    `a society`
    `a company`
    `a firm`
    `a partnership`
    `a trade union`
    `a municipality`
    `an association of persons`   -- (b)
    `a body that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "organization" (src:133-138)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 organization: the kind of body`
      `it is created for a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
      `it has an operational structure` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)
      `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 organization` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a public body` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a society` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a firm` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a trade union` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a municipality` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an association of persons` THEN IF `it is created for a common purpose` AND `it has an operational structure` AND `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an association of persons that (i) is created for a common purpose, (ii) has an operational structure, and (iii) holds itself out to the public as an association of persons"
    WHEN `a body that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "organization means"

-- peace officer includes (a) a mayor, warden, reeve, sheriff, deputy sheriff, sheriff’s officer and justice of the peace, (b) ..., (g). Limbs (c.1), (d), (e) and (f) apply only "when" or "while" the person is in the stated situation; the
-- person in the same office outside that situation is a separate member and is NOT COVERED (a marginal reading: see NOTES.md).
-- src:139 | peace officer includes
-- src:140 | (a) a mayor, warden, reeve, sheriff, deputy sheriff, sheriff’s officer and justice of the peace,
-- src:141 | (b) a member of the Correctional Service of Canada who is designated as a peace officer pursuant to Part I of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, and a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard and any other officer or permanent employee of a prison other than a penitentiary as defined in Part I of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act,
-- src:142 | (c) a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process,
-- src:143 | (c.1) a designated officer as defined in section 2 of the Integrated Cross-border Law Enforcement Operations Act, when
-- src:144 | (i) participating in an integrated cross-border operation, as defined in section 2 of that Act, or
-- src:145 | (ii) engaging in an activity incidental to such an operation, including travel for the purpose of participating in the operation and appearances in court arising from the operation,
-- src:146 | (d) an officer within the meaning of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001, or a person having the powers of such an officer, when performing any duty in the administration of any of those Acts,
-- src:147 | (d.1) an officer authorized under subsection 138(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act,
-- src:148 | (e) a person designated as a fishery guardian under the Fisheries Act when performing any duties or functions under that Act and a person designated as a fishery officer under the Fisheries Act when performing any duties or functions under that Act or the Coastal Fisheries Protection Act,
-- src:149 | (f) the pilot in command of an aircraft
-- src:150 | (i) registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or
-- src:151 | (ii) leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft registered in Canada under those regulations,
-- src:152 | while the aircraft is in flight, and
-- src:153 | (g) officers and non-commissioned members of the Canadian Forces who are
-- src:154 | (i) appointed for the purposes of section 156 of the National Defence Act, or
-- src:155 | (ii) employed on duties that the Governor in Council, in regulations made under the National Defence Act for the purposes of this paragraph, has prescribed to be of such a kind as to necessitate that the officers and non-commissioned members performing them have the powers of peace officers; (agent de la paix)
@ref s 2 "peace officer" (src:139-155)
DECLARE `s 2 peace officer capacity` IS ONE OF
    `a mayor`   -- (a)
    `a warden named in paragraph (a)`
    `a reeve`
    `a sheriff`
    `a deputy sheriff`
    `a sheriff’s officer`
    `a justice of the peace named in paragraph (a)`
    `a member of the Correctional Service of Canada who is designated as a peace officer pursuant to Part I of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`   -- (b)
    `a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard or other officer or permanent employee of a prison other than a penitentiary as defined in Part I of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`   -- (b)
    `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process`   -- (c)
    `a designated officer as defined in section 2 of the Integrated Cross-border Law Enforcement Operations Act, when participating in an integrated cross-border operation or engaging in an activity incidental to such an operation`   -- (c.1)
    `a designated officer as defined in section 2 of the Integrated Cross-border Law Enforcement Operations Act, when neither participating in an integrated cross-border operation nor engaging in an activity incidental to such an operation`
    `an officer within the meaning of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001, or a person having the powers of such an officer, when performing any duty in the administration of any of those Acts`   -- (d)
    `an officer within the meaning of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001, or a person having the powers of such an officer, when not performing any duty in the administration of any of those Acts`
    `an officer authorized under subsection 138(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`   -- (d.1)
    `a person designated as a fishery guardian or fishery officer under the Fisheries Act, when performing any duties or functions under that Act (or, for a fishery officer, the Coastal Fisheries Protection Act)`   -- (e)
    `a person designated as a fishery guardian or fishery officer under the Fisheries Act, when not performing any duties or functions under that Act or the Coastal Fisheries Protection Act`
    `the pilot in command of an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or leased without crew and operated by a person qualified to register such an aircraft in Canada, while the aircraft is in flight`   -- (f)
    `the pilot in command of such an aircraft while it is not in flight`
    `an officer or non-commissioned member of the Canadian Forces appointed for the purposes of section 156 of the National Defence Act`   -- (g)(i)
    `an officer or non-commissioned member of the Canadian Forces employed on duties prescribed by the Governor in Council, in regulations made under the National Defence Act, to be of such a kind as to necessitate the powers of peace officers`   -- (g)(ii)
    `a person in a capacity that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "peace officer" (src:139-155)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 peace officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `a mayor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a warden named in paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a reeve` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a sheriff` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a deputy sheriff` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a sheriff’s officer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a justice of the peace named in paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the Correctional Service of Canada who is designated as a peace officer pursuant to Part I of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard or other officer or permanent employee of a prison other than a penitentiary as defined in Part I of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a designated officer as defined in section 2 of the Integrated Cross-border Law Enforcement Operations Act, when participating in an integrated cross-border operation or engaging in an activity incidental to such an operation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a designated officer as defined in section 2 of the Integrated Cross-border Law Enforcement Operations Act, when neither participating in an integrated cross-border operation nor engaging in an activity incidental to such an operation` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when" participating in an integrated cross-border operation or engaging in an incidental activity
    WHEN `an officer within the meaning of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001, or a person having the powers of such an officer, when performing any duty in the administration of any of those Acts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an officer within the meaning of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001, or a person having the powers of such an officer, when not performing any duty in the administration of any of those Acts` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when performing any duty in the administration of any of those Acts"
    WHEN `an officer authorized under subsection 138(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person designated as a fishery guardian or fishery officer under the Fisheries Act, when performing any duties or functions under that Act (or, for a fishery officer, the Coastal Fisheries Protection Act)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person designated as a fishery guardian or fishery officer under the Fisheries Act, when not performing any duties or functions under that Act or the Coastal Fisheries Protection Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when performing any duties or functions under that Act"
    WHEN `the pilot in command of an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act, or leased without crew and operated by a person qualified to register such an aircraft in Canada, while the aircraft is in flight` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the pilot in command of such an aircraft while it is not in flight` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "while the aircraft is in flight"
    WHEN `an officer or non-commissioned member of the Canadian Forces appointed for the purposes of section 156 of the National Defence Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an officer or non-commissioned member of the Canadian Forces employed on duties prescribed by the Governor in Council, in regulations made under the National Defence Act, to be of such a kind as to necessitate the powers of peace officers` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person in a capacity that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "peace officer includes"

