-- prosecutor means the Attorney General or, where the Attorney General does not intervene, means the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies, and includes counsel acting on behalf of either of them.
-- src:161 | prosecutor means the Attorney General or, where the Attorney General does not intervene, means the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies, and includes counsel acting on behalf of either of them; (poursuivant)
@ref s 2 "prosecutor" (src:161)
DECLARE `s 2 prosecutor: who the person is` IS ONE OF
    `the Attorney General, as section 2 defines that term`
    `the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies, where the Attorney General does not intervene`
    `the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies, where the Attorney General intervenes`
    `counsel acting on behalf of the Attorney General`
    `counsel acting on behalf of the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies`
    `a person who is none of those`

@ref s 2 "prosecutor" (src:161)
GIVEN who IS A `s 2 prosecutor: who the person is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 prosecutor` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `the Attorney General, as section 2 defines that term` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies, where the Attorney General does not intervene` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies, where the Attorney General intervenes` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the Attorney General does not intervene"
    WHEN `counsel acting on behalf of the Attorney General` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `counsel acting on behalf of the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prosecutor means the Attorney General or, where the Attorney General does not intervene, means the person who institutes proceedings to which this Act applies"

-- provincial court judge means a person appointed or authorized to act by or pursuant to an Act of the legislature of a province, by whatever title, who has the power and authority of two or more justices of the peace, and includes the lawful deputy of that person.
-- src:162 | provincial court judge means a person appointed or authorized to act by or pursuant to an Act of the legislature of a province, by whatever title that person may be designated, who has the power and authority of two or more justices of the peace and includes the lawful deputy of that person; (juge de la cour provinciale)
@ref s 2 "provincial court judge" (src:162)
GIVEN `the person is appointed or authorized to act by or pursuant to an Act of the legislature of a province, by whatever title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the power and authority of two or more justices of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the lawful deputy of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF (`the person is appointed or authorized to act by or pursuant to an Act of the legislature of a province, by whatever title` AND `the person has the power and authority of two or more justices of the peace`)
        OR `the person is the lawful deputy of such a person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provincial court judge means a person appointed or authorized to act by or pursuant to an Act of the legislature of a province, by whatever title that person may be designated, who has the power and authority of two or more justices of the peace"

