-- senior officer means a representative who plays an important role in the establishment of an organization’s policies or is responsible for managing an important aspect of the organization’s activities and, in the case of a body corporate, includes a director, its chief executive officer and its chief financial officer.
-- src:177 | senior officer means a representative who plays an important role in the establishment of an organization’s policies or is responsible for managing an important aspect of the organization’s activities and, in the case of a body corporate, includes a director, its chief executive officer and its chief financial officer; (cadre supérieur)
@ref s 2 "senior officer" (src:177)
GIVEN `the person is a representative, by s 2 representative` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person plays an important role in the establishment of the organization’s policies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible for managing an important aspect of the organization’s activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organization is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director, or the chief executive officer or the chief financial officer, of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
