-- summons means, unless a contrary intention appears, a summons in Form 6 issued by a judge or justice or by the chairperson of a Review Board as defined in subsection 672.1(1).
-- FORK: when "a contrary intention appears" the definition is displaced and the text does not say what the word then means: NOTHING (the other reading is JUST FALSE).
-- src:181 | summons means, unless a contrary intention appears, a summons in Form 6 issued by a judge or justice or by the chairperson of a Review Board as defined in subsection 672.1(1); (sommation)
@ref s 2 "summons" (src:181)
DECLARE `s 2 summons: who issued it` IS ONE OF
    `issued by a judge`
    `issued by a justice`
    `issued by the chairperson of a Review Board as defined in subsection 672.1(1)`
    `issued by someone else`

@ref s 2 "summons" (src:181)
GIVEN `it is a summons in Form 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      issuer IS A `s 2 summons: who issued it`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 summons` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless a contrary intention appears"
    ELSE IF NOT `it is a summons in Form 6`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "summons means, unless a contrary intention appears, a summons in Form 6"
         ELSE CONSIDER issuer
              WHEN `issued by a judge` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `issued by a justice` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `issued by the chairperson of a Review Board as defined in subsection 672.1(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `issued by someone else` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a summons in Form 6 issued by a judge or justice or by the chairperson of a Review Board"

-- territorial division includes any province, county, union of counties, township, city, town, parish or other judicial division or place to which the context applies.
-- src:190 | territorial division includes any province, county, union of counties, township, city, town, parish or other judicial division or place to which the context applies; (circonscription territoriale)
@ref s 2 "territorial division" (src:190)
DECLARE `s 2 territorial division kind` IS ONE OF
    `a province as a territorial division`
    `a county as a territorial division`
    `a union of counties`
    `a township as a territorial division`
    `a city as a territorial division`
    `a town as a territorial division`
    `a parish as a territorial division`
    `another judicial division or place to which the context applies`
    `a place to which the context does not apply`
    `a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "territorial division" (src:190)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 territorial division kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 territorial division` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a province as a territorial division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a county as a territorial division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a union of counties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a township as a territorial division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a city as a territorial division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a town as a territorial division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a parish as a territorial division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another judicial division or place to which the context applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a place to which the context does not apply` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or place to which the context applies"
    WHEN `a thing that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "territorial division includes"

-- terrorism offence means (a) an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 or 83.18 to 83.23, (b) an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group,
-- (c) an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament where the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, or (d) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c).
-- Section numbers are decimals, so "83.02 to 83.04" includes 83.03, 83.031 to 83.0392 and 83.04, and "83.18 to 83.23" includes 83.181, 83.19, 83.191, 83.2, 83.201, 83.202, 83.21, 83.22, 83.221, 83.222, 83.223 and 83.23.
-- src:191 | terrorism offence means
-- src:192 | (a) an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 or 83.18 to 83.23,
-- src:193 | (b) an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group,
-- src:194 | (c) an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament where the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, or
-- src:195 | (d) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c); (infraction de terrorisme)
@ref s 2 "terrorism offence" (src:191-195)
GIVEN form IS A `s 2 form of the charge`
      `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `it is an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 terrorism offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `the offence itself` THEN `paragraph (a), (b) or (c) holds`
    WHEN `a conspiracy to commit the offence` THEN `paragraph (a), (b) or (c) holds`   -- (d)
    WHEN `an attempt to commit the offence` THEN `paragraph (a), (b) or (c) holds`
    WHEN `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence` THEN `paragraph (a), (b) or (c) holds`
    WHEN `counselling in relation to the offence` THEN `paragraph (a), (b) or (c) holds`
    WHEN `a form of participation that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorism offence means"
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the offence charged, or the offence the charge concerns`'s `section`
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS
            (`the section` AT LEAST 83.02 AND `the section` AT MOST 83.04) OR (`the section` AT LEAST 83.18 AND `the section` AT MOST 83.23)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            IF `it is an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` AND `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group`
            THEN `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group"
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            IF `it is an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament`
            THEN `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament where the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity"
        `paragraph (a), (b) or (c) holds` MEANS
            IF `paragraph (a) holds` OR (`paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE IF (`paragraph (b)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`paragraph (c)` EQUALS NOTHING)
                 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a terrorist group, or the act a terrorist activity, is for s 83.01(1) and is not determined
                 ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorism offence means"

-- terrorist activity has the same meaning as in subsection 83.01(1): the definition is in another part. Its answer is taken as an input, named for that section.
-- src:196 | terrorist activity has the same meaning as in subsection 83.01(1); (activité terroriste)
@ref s 2 "terrorist activity" (src:196)
GIVEN `the act or omission is a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 terrorist activity` MEANS `the act or omission is a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)`

-- terrorist group has the same meaning as in subsection 83.01(1): the definition is in another part. Its answer is taken as an input, named for that section.
-- src:197 | terrorist group has the same meaning as in subsection 83.01(1); (groupe terroriste)
@ref s 2 "terrorist group" (src:197)
GIVEN `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 terrorist group` MEANS `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`

-- testamentary instrument includes any will, codicil or other testamentary writing or appointment, during the life of the testator ... and after his death, whether it relates to real or personal property or to both.
-- src:198 | testamentary instrument includes any will, codicil or other testamentary writing or appointment, during the life of the testator whose testamentary disposition it purports to be and after his death, whether it relates to real or personal property or to both; (acte testamentaire)
@ref s 2 "testamentary instrument" (src:198)
DECLARE `s 2 testamentary instrument kind` IS ONE OF
    `a will`
    `a codicil`
    `another testamentary writing`
    `a testamentary appointment`
    `a document that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "testamentary instrument" (src:198)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 testamentary instrument kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 testamentary instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a codicil` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another testamentary writing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a testamentary appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "testamentary instrument includes"

-- trustee means a person declared by any Act to be a trustee or who is, by the law of a province, a trustee, and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, includes a trustee on an express trust created by deed, will or instrument in writing, or by parol.
-- src:199 | trustee means a person who is declared by any Act to be a trustee or is, by the law of a province, a trustee, and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, includes a trustee on an express trust created by deed, will or instrument in writing, or by parol; (fiduciaire)
@ref s 2 "trustee" (src:199)
DECLARE `s 2 trustee basis` IS ONE OF
    `a person who is declared by any Act to be a trustee`
    `a person who is, by the law of a province, a trustee`
    `a trustee on an express trust created by deed`
    `a trustee on an express trust created by will`
    `a trustee on an express trust created by instrument in writing`
    `a trustee on an express trust created by parol`
    `a person who is none of those`

@ref s 2 "trustee" (src:199)
GIVEN basis IS A `s 2 trustee basis`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 trustee` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `a person who is declared by any Act to be a trustee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who is, by the law of a province, a trustee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a trustee on an express trust created by deed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a trustee on an express trust created by will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a trustee on an express trust created by instrument in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a trustee on an express trust created by parol` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "without restricting the generality of the foregoing"

-- undertaking means, unless a contrary intention appears, an undertaking in Form 10 given to a peace officer. FORK: as for `s 2 summons`, a contrary intention gives NOTHING.
-- src:200 | undertaking means, unless a contrary intention appears, an undertaking in Form 10 given to a peace officer; (promesse)
@ref s 2 "undertaking" (src:200)
GIVEN `it is an undertaking in Form 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was given to a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 undertaking` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless a contrary intention appears"
    ELSE IF NOT `it is an undertaking in Form 10`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "undertaking means, unless a contrary intention appears, an undertaking in Form 10 given to a peace officer"
         ELSE `it was given to a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE for "given to a peace officer" unmet; NOTHING when the recipient's status is itself undetermined

-- unfit to stand trial means unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered or to instruct counsel to do so, and, in particular, unable on account of mental disorder to (a) understand the nature or object of the proceedings,
-- (b) understand the possible consequences of the proceedings, or (c) communicate with counsel. "In particular" is read as naming cases that suffice (a marginal reading: they would also suffice if read as mere illustrations of the general inability).
-- src:201 | unfit to stand trial means unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered or to instruct counsel to do so, and, in particular, unable on account of mental disorder to
-- src:202 | (a) understand the nature or object of the proceedings,
-- src:203 | (b) understand the possible consequences of the proceedings, or
-- src:204 | (c) communicate with counsel; (inaptitude à subir son procès)
@ref s 2 "unfit to stand trial" (src:201-204)
GIVEN `unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable on account of mental disorder to instruct counsel to conduct a defence at any such stage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable on account of mental disorder to understand the nature or object of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `unable on account of mental disorder to understand the possible consequences of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `unable on account of mental disorder to communicate with counsel` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 unfit to stand trial` MEANS
    IF     `unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered`
        OR `unable on account of mental disorder to instruct counsel to conduct a defence at any such stage`
        OR `unable on account of mental disorder to understand the nature or object of the proceedings`
        OR `unable on account of mental disorder to understand the possible consequences of the proceedings`
        OR `unable on account of mental disorder to communicate with counsel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unfit to stand trial means unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered or to instruct counsel to do so"

-- United Nations operation means an operation that is established by the competent organ of the United Nations in accordance with the Charter and is conducted under United Nations authority and control, if it is for the purpose of maintaining or restoring international peace and security
-- or if the Security Council or the General Assembly has declared an exceptional risk to the safety of the personnel. It does not include a Chapter VII enforcement action in which any of the personnel are engaged as combatants against organized armed forces and to which the law of international armed conflict applies.
-- src:205 | United Nations operation means an operation that is established by the competent organ of the United Nations in accordance with the Charter of the United Nations and is conducted under United Nations authority and control, if the operation is for the purpose of maintaining or restoring international peace and security or if the Security Council or the General Assembly of the United Nations has declared, for the purposes of the Convention on the Safety of United Nations and Associated Personnel, that there exists an exceptional risk to the safety of the personnel participating in the operation. It does not include an operation authorized by the Security Council as an enforcement action under Chapter VII of the Charter of the United Nations in which any of the personnel are engaged as combatants against organized armed forces and to which the law of international armed conflict applies; (opération des Nations Unies)
@ref s 2 "United Nations operation" (src:205)
GIVEN `it is established by the competent organ of the United Nations in accordance with the Charter of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conducted under United Nations authority and control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of maintaining or restoring international peace and security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Security Council or the General Assembly has declared, for the purposes of the Convention on the Safety of United Nations and Associated Personnel, that there exists an exceptional risk to the safety of the personnel participating in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an operation authorized by the Security Council as an enforcement action under Chapter VII of the Charter in which any of the personnel are engaged as combatants against organized armed forces and to which the law of international armed conflict applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 United Nations operation` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `it is established by the competent organ of the United Nations in accordance with the Charter of the United Nations`
            AND `it is conducted under United Nations authority and control`
            AND (   `it is for the purpose of maintaining or restoring international peace and security`
                 OR `the Security Council or the General Assembly has declared, for the purposes of the Convention on the Safety of United Nations and Associated Personnel, that there exists an exceptional risk to the safety of the personnel participating in it`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the operation is for the purpose of maintaining or restoring international peace and security or if the Security Council or the General Assembly of the United Nations has declared"
    ELSE IF `it is an operation authorized by the Security Council as an enforcement action under Chapter VII of the Charter in which any of the personnel are engaged as combatants against organized armed forces and to which the law of international armed conflict applies`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It does not include an operation authorized by the Security Council as an enforcement action under Chapter VII of the Charter of the United Nations"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- United Nations personnel means (a) persons engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General as members of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation, or (b) any other officials or experts on mission of the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies or the IAEA who are present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted.
-- src:206 | United Nations personnel means
-- src:207 | (a) persons who are engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as members of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation, or
-- src:208 | (b) any other officials or experts who are on mission of the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies or the International Atomic Energy Agency and who are present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted; (personnel des Nations Unies)
@ref s 2 "United Nations personnel" (src:206-208)
DECLARE `s 2 United Nations personnel basis` IS ONE OF
    `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation`   -- (a)
    `an official or expert on mission of the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies or the International Atomic Energy Agency who is present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted`   -- (b)
    `an official or expert on mission of the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies or the International Atomic Energy Agency who is not present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted`
    `a person who is none of those`

@ref s 2 "United Nations personnel" (src:206-208)
GIVEN basis IS A `s 2 United Nations personnel basis`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 United Nations personnel` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `a person engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General of the United Nations as a member of the military, police or civilian components of a United Nations operation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an official or expert on mission of the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies or the International Atomic Energy Agency who is present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an official or expert on mission of the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies or the International Atomic Energy Agency who is not present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who are present in an official capacity in the area where a United Nations operation is conducted"
    WHEN `a person who is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "United Nations personnel means"

-- valuable mineral means a mineral of a value of at least $100 per kilogram, and includes precious metals, diamonds and other gemstones and any rock or ore that contains those minerals.
-- src:209 | valuable mineral means a mineral of a value of at least $100 per kilogram, and includes precious metals, diamonds and other gemstones and any rock or ore that contains those minerals; (minéraux précieux)
@ref s 2 "valuable mineral" (src:209)
DECLARE `s 2 valuable mineral kind` IS ONE OF
    `a mineral`
    `a precious metal`
    `a diamond or other gemstone`
    `a rock or ore that contains those minerals`
    `a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "valuable mineral" (src:209)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
      `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 valuable mineral` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a mineral` THEN IF `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` AT LEAST 100 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a mineral of a value of at least $100 per kilogram"
    WHEN `a precious metal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a diamond or other gemstone` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a rock or ore that contains those minerals` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valuable mineral means a mineral of a value of at least $100 per kilogram"

-- valuable security includes (a) an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person (i) to a share or interest in a public stock or fund ..., or (ii) to a deposit in a financial institution,
-- (b) any debenture, deed, bond, bill, note, warrant, order or other security for money or for payment of money, (c) a document of title to lands or goods wherever situated, (d) a stamp or writing that secures or evidences title to or an interest in a chattel personal ..., and (e) a release, receipt, discharge or other instrument evidencing payment of money.
-- src:210 | valuable security includes
-- src:211 | (a) an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person
-- src:212 | (i) to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society, or
-- src:213 | (ii) to a deposit in a financial institution,
-- src:214 | (b) any debenture, deed, bond, bill, note, warrant, order or other security for money or for payment of money,
-- src:215 | (c) a document of title to lands or goods wherever situated,
-- src:216 | (d) a stamp or writing that secures or evidences title to or an interest in a chattel personal, or that evidences delivery of a chattel personal, and
-- src:217 | (e) a release, receipt, discharge or other instrument evidencing payment of money; (valeur ou effet appréciable)
@ref s 2 "valuable security" (src:210-217)
DECLARE `s 2 valuable security kind` IS ONE OF
    `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society`   -- (a)(i)
    `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a deposit in a financial institution`   -- (a)(ii)
    `a debenture, deed, bond, bill, note, warrant, order or other security for money or for payment of money`   -- (b)
    `a document of title to lands or goods wherever situated`   -- (c)
    `a stamp or writing that secures or evidences title to or an interest in a chattel personal, or that evidences delivery of a chattel personal`   -- (d)
    `a release, receipt, discharge or other instrument evidencing payment of money`   -- (e)
    `an instrument that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "valuable security" (src:210-217)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 valuable security kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 valuable security` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a share or interest in a public stock or fund or in any fund of a body corporate, company or society` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an order, exchequer acquittance or other security that entitles or evidences the title of any person to a deposit in a financial institution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a debenture, deed, bond, bill, note, warrant, order or other security for money or for payment of money` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document of title to lands or goods wherever situated` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a stamp or writing that secures or evidences title to or an interest in a chattel personal, or that evidences delivery of a chattel personal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a release, receipt, discharge or other instrument evidencing payment of money` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "valuable security includes"

-- victim means a person against whom an offence has been committed, or is alleged to have been committed, who has suffered, or is alleged to have suffered, physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result, and includes, for the purposes of sections 672.5, 722 and 745.63,
-- a person who has suffered such harm as the result of the commission of an offence against any other person. The extension is limited to those three sections: a person harmed by an offence against another, outside them, is NOT COVERED (a marginal reading: the other reading is JUST FALSE).
-- src:218 | victim means a person against whom an offence has been committed, or is alleged to have been committed, who has suffered, or is alleged to have suffered, physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission or alleged commission of the offence and includes, for the purposes of sections 672.5, 722 and 745.63, a person who has suffered physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission of an offence against any other person. (victime)
@ref s 2 "victim" (src:218)
GIVEN `an offence has been committed, or is alleged to have been committed, against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has suffered, or is alleged to have suffered, physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission or alleged commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is section 672.5, 722 or 745.63` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has suffered physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission of an offence against any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 victim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an offence has been committed, or is alleged to have been committed, against the person` AND `the person has suffered, or is alleged to have suffered, physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission or alleged commission of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the purpose is section 672.5, 722 or 745.63` AND `the person has suffered physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission of an offence against any other person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `the purpose is section 672.5, 722 or 745.63`) AND `the person has suffered physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss as the result of the commission of an offence against any other person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of sections 672.5, 722 and 745.63"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "victim means a person against whom an offence has been committed, or is alleged to have been committed, who has suffered, or is alleged to have suffered, physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss"

-- videoconference means any means of telecommunication that allows the judge, justice or chairperson of a Review Board, as defined in subsection 672.1(1), and any individual to engage in simultaneous visual and oral communication in a proceeding.
-- src:219 | videoconference means any means of telecommunication that allows the judge, justice or chairperson of a Review Board, as defined in subsection 672.1(1), and any individual to engage in simultaneous visual and oral communication in a proceeding; (vidéoconférence)
@ref s 2 "videoconference" (src:219)
GIVEN `it is a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it allows the judge, justice or chairperson of a Review Board, as defined in subsection 672.1(1), and any individual to engage in simultaneous visual and oral communication in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 videoconference` MEANS
    IF `it is a means of telecommunication` AND `it allows the judge, justice or chairperson of a Review Board, as defined in subsection 672.1(1), and any individual to engage in simultaneous visual and oral communication in a proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "videoconference means any means of telecommunication that allows the judge, justice or chairperson of a Review Board"

-- weapon means any thing used, designed to be used or intended for use (a) in causing death or injury to any person, or (b) for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing,
-- includes a firearm and, for the purposes of sections 88, 267 and 272, any thing used, designed to be used or intended for use in binding or tying up a person against their will.
-- src:220 | weapon means any thing used, designed to be used or intended for use
-- src:221 | (a) in causing death or injury to any person, or
-- src:222 | (b) for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person
-- src:223 | and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, includes a firearm and, for the purposes of sections 88, 267 and 272, any thing used, designed to be used or intended for use in binding or tying up a person against their will; (arme)
@ref s 2 "weapon" (src:220-223)
GIVEN `it is used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it is used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it is a firearm, by s 2 firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is used, designed to be used or intended for use in binding or tying up a person against their will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is section 88, 267 or 272` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 weapon` MEANS
    IF     `it is used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person`
        OR `it is used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person`
        OR (`it is a firearm, by s 2 firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        OR (`it is used, designed to be used or intended for use in binding or tying up a person against their will` AND `the purpose is section 88, 267 or 272`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "without restricting the generality of the foregoing"

-- wreck includes the cargo, stores and tackle of a vessel and all parts of a vessel separated from the vessel, and the property of persons who belong to, are on board or have quitted a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress at any place in Canada.
-- src:224 | wreck includes the cargo, stores and tackle of a vessel and all parts of a vessel separated from the vessel, and the property of persons who belong to, are on board or have quitted a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress at any place in Canada; (épave)
@ref s 2 "wreck" (src:224)
DECLARE `s 2 wreck kind` IS ONE OF
    `the cargo of a vessel`
    `the stores of a vessel`
    `the tackle of a vessel`
    `a part of a vessel separated from the vessel`
    `the property of a person who belongs to, is on board or has quitted a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress at any place in Canada`
    `a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "wreck" (src:224)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 wreck kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 wreck` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the cargo of a vessel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the stores of a vessel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the tackle of a vessel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a part of a vessel separated from the vessel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the property of a person who belongs to, is on board or has quitted a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress at any place in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "wreck includes"

-- writing includes a document of any kind and any mode in which, and any material on which, words or figures, whether at length or abridged, are written, printed or otherwise expressed, or a map or plan is inscribed.
-- src:225 | writing includes a document of any kind and any mode in which, and any material on which, words or figures, whether at length or abridged, are written, printed or otherwise expressed, or a map or plan is inscribed. (écrit)
@ref s 2 "writing" (src:225)
DECLARE `s 2 writing kind` IS ONE OF
    `a document of any kind`
    `any mode in which, or any material on which, words or figures, whether at length or abridged, are written, printed or otherwise expressed`
    `any mode in which, or any material on which, a map or plan is inscribed`
    `a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 2 "writing" (src:225)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2 writing kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 writing` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a document of any kind` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any mode in which, or any material on which, words or figures, whether at length or abridged, are written, printed or otherwise expressed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any mode in which, or any material on which, a map or plan is inscribed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "writing includes"

§ `Section 2.1 -- Further definitions: firearms`

-- 2.1 In this Act, ammunition, antique firearm, ... restricted weapon, as well as authorization, licence and registration certificate when used in relation to those words and expressions, have the same meaning as in subsection 84(1).
-- The meaning is in subsection 84(1), in another part: its answer is taken as an input, named for that section; for a term this section does not name, nothing is said.
-- src:227 | 2.1 In this Act, ammunition, antique firearm, automatic firearm, cartridge magazine, cross-bow, firearm part, handgun, imitation firearm, prohibited ammunition, prohibited device, prohibited firearm, prohibited weapon, replica firearm, restricted firearm and restricted weapon, as well as authorization, licence and registration certificate when used in relation to those words and expressions, have the same meaning as in subsection 84(1).
@ref s 2.1 (src:227)
DECLARE `s 2.1 term` IS ONE OF
    `ammunition`
    `antique firearm`
    `automatic firearm`
    `cartridge magazine`
    `cross-bow`
    `firearm part`
    `handgun`
    `imitation firearm`
    `prohibited ammunition`
    `prohibited device`
    `prohibited firearm`
    `prohibited weapon`
    `replica firearm`
    `restricted firearm`
    `restricted weapon`
    `authorization, when used in relation to those words and expressions`
    `licence, when used in relation to those words and expressions`
    `registration certificate, when used in relation to those words and expressions`
    `authorization, licence or registration certificate, when used in relation to some other word or expression`
    `a term that section 2.1 does not name`

@ref s 2.1 (src:227)
GIVEN term IS A `s 2.1 term`
      `the thing is within the meaning of the term in subsection 84(1), by s 84(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2.1 the term has the meaning it has in subsection 84(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `authorization, licence or registration certificate, when used in relation to some other word or expression` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when used in relation to those words and expressions"
    WHEN `a term that section 2.1 does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): section 2.1 names the terms above and no others
    OTHERWISE `the thing is within the meaning of the term in subsection 84(1), by s 84(1)`   -- the answer of s 84(1) for each of the fifteen terms and for authorization, licence and registration certificate used in relation to them
